{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"Module 08 — Endpoint Security: IoT Devices\nDevice → Comm → Cloud → Process · Attacks → Measures → Standards","x":-560,"y":-2330,"width":410,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"IoT Basics (LO01)\nIoT/IoE: web-enabled sensing devices\n\"thing\" = device embedded on objects\n3-D plane: anyone/anytime, outdoor/indoor,\non the move, away from PC\nH2H · H2T · T2T interaction\n4 systems: sensing · gateways · cloud storage\n· mobile remote-control apps\nApplications: smart buildings, IIoT (3 growth\napproaches), healthcare, transportation,\nretail, IT/networks","x":-1650,"y":-2120,"width":370,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"Ecosystem + Architecture (LO02)\nBlocks: gateway/cloud gateway, streaming\nprocessors, data lakes, big data warehouse,\nanalytics, ML, control apps (rule/ML), user apps\n4 layers: Device → Communication → Cloud\nPlatform → Process\n4 communication models: Device-to-Device ·\nDevice-to-Cloud · Device-to-Gateway · Back-end\nData-Sharing (cloud-to-cloud)\nProtocols: ZigBee/Z-Wave, IEEE 802.15.4,\nCoAP/MQTT, OAuth 2.0, JSON","x":-1650,"y":-1820,"width":370,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b3","type":"text","text":"Challenges + Risks (LO03)\nChallenges: scale, never-turned-off devices,\ndeployed without IT oversight, 5G bandwidth\n→ botnets/DDoS, SCA on low-cost hardware\n12 inherent issues (no security/privacy, default/\nhardcoded creds, cleartext + open ports, coding\nerrors, physical theft, no vendor support)\nThreat map per layer: device/communication/\ncloud/process\nOWASP Top 10 IoT: #1 weak/hardcoded\npasswords · #2 insecure network services ·#5\nno secure updates","x":-1650,"y":-1520,"width":370,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b4","type":"text","text":"Device Layer (LO04a/b)\nAttacks: node tampering, jamming/RF\ninterference, malicious node injection, tag\ncloning, code injection, replay, timing/SCA,\neavesdropping, object replication, hardware\ntrojan, outage\nCtr: FHSS/spread spectrum, Perrig lightweight\nauth, AES/Elliptic-Curve per-node ACLs","x":-1650,"y":-1210,"width":370,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b5","type":"text","text":"Communication Layer (LO04c)\nRFID: relay (distance-bounding), crypto,\nDoS · NFC: relay/tag clone, RF shielding\nBluetooth: Bluesnarfing, BlueBugging,\nBluejacking, BlueSmack, Car Whisperer, KNOB\nWi-Fi: WEP (Korek/Chopchop/Fragmentation/\nFMS/PTW), Michael/TKIP → CCMP/AES/IPsec\nZigBee: KillerBee · AES-128\nZ-Wave: S2 · RPL: DOG · 6LoWPAN: DoS/frag\nTCP/UDP: SYN flood, UDP flood, XMAS, Smurf\nCoAP/MQTT: amplification → TLS/DTLS + tokens","x":-1650,"y":-920,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b6","type":"text","text":"Cloud + Process (LO04d)\nCloud attacks: account/theft, data-in-transit/at-\nrest compromise, key/cert storage attacks,\nmalware injection, botnets, backdoor/DoS,\ncloud service interruption\nCtr: TLS 1.2/IPsec/DTLS + subnet firewall ACLs,\nAES-256 at rest, HSM key mgmt, mutual auth,\nSELinux + SDP, digital signatures\nProcess: governance, audits, training, IR","x":-1150,"y":-2120,"width":410,"height":210,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b7","type":"text","text":"27 Security Measures (LO05, M01-M14)\nM01-M05 visibility: AssetExplorer/ServiceNow asset\nmaps (Oracle) · behavior monitoring (Domotz Pro)\nM06-M10 access: PACL/VACL · malware (Mirai, Echobot)\n· scanning (Nexpose, RloT Scanner, beSTORM) · firmware\nOTA · close services (nmap -sS -sU -O)\nM11-M14 crypto/hardware: E2EE (TLS 1.2, IPsec, DTLS,\nAES-256) · identity (X.509, mTLS, PKI) · strong auth\n(MFA) · chip-level (TPM 2.0, RoT) · HSM (SGX/TrustZone)","x":-1150,"y":-1830,"width":420,"height":230,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b8","type":"text","text":"27 Security Measures (LO05, M15-M27)\nM15-M19: gateways · control server · remote admin\n(SSH + Unplug n' Pray) · router (WPA2/WPA3, WPS/\nUPnP off, Zenmap/ShieldsUP)\nM20-M27: Wi-Fi isolation (pcWRT guest) · Ethernet\nisolation (VLAN X1/X2/X3) · internet-access whitelist ·\nnetwork activity (pcWRT) · bandwidth (SolarWinds NPM/\nNTA, PRTG) · centralize logs (Cloud IoT Core + Stackdriver)\n· public-Wi-Fi security · shadow IoT (Shodan)","x":-1150,"y":-1510,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b9","type":"text","text":"Tools + Best Practices (LO06)\nChecklist: device (secure boot, change defaults,\ndisable Telnet 23, monitor 48101) · network\n(segment) · overall (Lock Out, updates, geo)\nSeaCat.io (Teskalabs mTLS tunnel, port 48101,\nNginx 443) · DigiCert IoT Security (mTLS fleet)\nMore: PwnPulse, Allot, Cisco IoT TD, SecEdge,\nnet-Shield, Noddos, AWS IoT Device Defender,\nTrustwave EPS, Subex, libsecurity-go","x":-1150,"y":-1210,"width":420,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b10","type":"text","text":"Standards + Initiatives (LO07)\nAIOTI: 17+2 WGs (WG01 research → WG09\nprivacy/security)\nNIST: 8 security-function areas (asset ID, dev\nconfig, data protection, updates, monitoring,\nhardening)\nDHS 6 principles: security by design, updates/\nvuln mgmt, recognized practices, prioritize by\nimpact, transparency, connect deliberately\nGSMA: 85 recommendations + assessment 8\nareas (secure boot, storage, key mgmt, OTA,\napp isolation, DDoS, privacy, attack mitigation)\nStandards: CWE, CAPEC, FIPS 140-3, Common\nCriteria ISO/IEC 15408 (EAL 1-7)","x":-1150,"y":-900,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"flow","type":"text","text":"Flow\nUnderstand device + ecosystem → map risks by\nlayer → harden every layer: device →\ncommunication → cloud → process → apply the\n27 measures → tool up → follow standards\nSecurity-by-design; never rely on default\ncredentials; keep devices visible, segmented,\nand patched (Zero Trust per-device keys).","x":-160,"y":-1900,"width":430,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"end","type":"text","text":"Module Summary points\n4-layer architecture + 4 communication models\nframe everything · every layer has its own\nattack taxonomy + countermeasures (device:\nphysical/tamper; communication: protocol-\nspecific; cloud/process: data + access) · the\n27 measures are the checklist · OWASP #1\n(weak/hardcoded passwords) + never-turned-\noff devices drive botnets/DDoS","x":540,"y":-1900,"width":430,"height":180,"color":"5"}
	],
